      "template": "The flood defence is {1}, with breach status {2} under {3}.\nThe area behind it is {4}; {5} warning time remains for {6}.\nRoutes are {7}, essential services are {8}, and the evidence consists of {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced European crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, water-authority and municipal services. Write an approximately 400-word, realistic exercise scenario and decision-support briefing about dam or levee damage or failure. Use every selected situation value, distinguish verified evidence from reports, and make the warning time and exposed communities clear without giving engineering instructions. If measures are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps; if no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. Address life safety, coordination, public information and continuity in a proportionate way. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions for decision-makers.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Damage reported beside the polder",
        "desc": "<p>Following high river discharge, a patrol reports damage to a flood defence beside a rural polder. No breach has been established; the first reports are unconfirmed and the shared picture is incomplete. Several hours may remain before dangerous water reaches dispersed households, but the estimate is being checked with the water authority.</p><p>Routes are restricted and local utility services are affected. The municipality and water authority open a liaison cell, explain the uncertainty to residents and prepare local reception facilities. Emergency repair staff are asked to assess the damaged section under the authority of the flood-defence manager; the exercise does not prescribe technical repair methods.</p><p>Teams prepare phased relocation if monitoring confirms worsening conditions. Medical rescue capacity is staged without treating a breach as a fact. Participants must agree what evidence would trigger a confirmed-breach evacuation alert, how to reach households if access deteriorates, and how to coordinate shelter and care support across the affected area.",
        "choices": [
          "toestand.schade",
          "bres.onzeker",
