      "template": "The building serves as {1} and is {2} to the public. The space is used for {3}.\nVisitors are admitted by {4}, with {5}. Visitors’ accessibility needs include {6}.\nService delivery is {7} and the public entrances are {8}. Visitors experience {9} as a result.\nBuilding management and the service provider coordinate through {10}. The alternative for visitors is {11}; they receive information {12}.",
      "prompt": "Create an English-language scenario about continuity and visitor care in a public building. Use all selected values concerning use, opening status, occupancy, accessibility needs, service disruption and alternative service delivery. Link decisions by building management and the service provider to clear information and the effects on visitors. Do not describe technical or physical vulnerabilities. End with two questions for the organisation.",
      "example": {
        "label": "The town hall remains accessible",
        "desc": "<p>A town hall receives visitors to its public service desk by appointment only, while one entrance remains open. Occupancy is moderate and service delivery is temporarily limited. Residents who struggle with digital services in particular face longer waits.</p><p>Building management and the service agree on an alternative at a joint meeting: anyone who cannot be seen receives a new appointment personally. This keeps essential services accessible without assuming that everyone can manage online.</p>",
