      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical and municipal services. Write an approximately 400-word realistic earthquake incident narrative for professional exercise and decision-support use, based only on the situation details supplied. Structure it with a concise incident overview, evolving hazards and exposure, effects on people and infrastructure, response capacity and uncertainties, then the operational picture. If measures are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps; do not imply that a selected action has succeeded unless the scenario says so. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions for participants. Use clear international British English and avoid unsupported technical certainty.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Aftershock rescue in a dense district",
