      "prompt": "You are an experienced European crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, utility and municipal services. Write an approximately 400-word realistic exercise scenario and decision-support briefing about a severe windstorm, tropical cyclone, tornado or convective storm. Use every selected situation value and distinguish forecast information from observed damage and service disruption. If measures are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps; if no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. Address warning, life safety, rescue access, vulnerable people and recovery without giving unsafe operational instructions. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Wind damage across an urban district",
        "desc": "<p>A severe windstorm has passed over a dense urban district after widespread damaging winds. Local damage and minor injuries are reported around transport links, while debris obstructs several routes. Power and communications are disrupted in some blocks, and one community has asked for help reaching isolated residents.</p><p>Regional crisis command aligns fire, police, ambulance, utility and municipal teams. Urban search-and-rescue teams assess reports of people trapped, medical triage is organised for injured residents, and a shelter opens for people displaced from damaged buildings. Public alerts share verified road closures and accessible shelter information without overstating unconfirmed reports.</p><p>Crews work to reopen emergency access routes and restore power at affected critical facilities. The exercise focuses on how to prioritise search reports, maintain care for vulnerable residents, and coordinate utility restoration alongside rescue. Participants should identify how the response would change if additional districts reported serious structural damage or if communications failed across the wider region.",
        "choices": [
          "storm-type.windstorm",
          "storm-phase.passed",
          "wind-severity.damaging",
          "storm-area.urban",
          "storm-population.community",
          "storm-assets.transport",
          "storm-damage.local",
          "storm-utilities.local",
          "storm-access.obstructed",
          "storm-rescue.urban",
          "storm-evacuation.displaced",
          "storm-medical.triage",
          "storm-command.regional",
          "storm-warning.alert",
          "storm-continuity.access"
        ]
      }
