      "template": "A grid failure caused by {1} affects {2}; restoration is {3}.\nThe affected area is {4}, with {5} and {6}.\nEssential services affected include {7}, community impact is {8}, and restoration capacity is {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, transport and municipal services. Write for incident commanders and crisis-management professionals. Create a realistic, approximately 400-word electricity network failure incident scenario for an exercise or decision-support briefing, based only on the selected situation details and any measures listed. Structure it as: initial situation and timeline; operational challenges and uncertainty; likely short-term developments and dependencies; coordination and communications; and a concise assessment. If measures are listed, including investigation measures if applicable, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and name important gaps without assuming they have already succeeded. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution or response plan. Keep the account plausible, neutral and suitable for an international European audience. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions for participants.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Regional winter outage",
        "desc": "<p>A substation equipment failure during a cold-weather evening peak interrupts electricity to several districts and surrounding rural communities. The utility expects repairs to take many hours, and initial switching attempts have not restored supply. Mobile coverage is becoming unreliable as backup batteries run down, while water operators report reduced pumping capacity.</p><p>Hospitals are on emergency generators, but care providers identify residents who rely on powered medical equipment at home. The utility dispatches specialist repair crews and isolates the failed substation section; municipal services open a warm support centre and begin welfare checks in the hardest-hit neighbourhoods.</p><p>Regional crisis command coordinates the electricity operator, health services, water providers, telecoms and local authorities. Public information explains safe generator use, food and medicine precautions, accessible support locations and uncertainty in restoration times. Participants consider prioritisation, dependencies between infrastructure, vulnerable-person support and how to manage a prolonged outage without overpromising restoration.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "grid-cause.substation-equipment-failure",
          "grid-footprint.several-districts",
          "grid-restoration.prolonged-restoration",
          "grid-area.dense-urban-area",
          "grid-demand.cold-weather-peak",
          "grid-infrastructure.accessible-local-network",
          "grid-services.water-or-wastewater-services-affected",
          "grid-people.vulnerable-people-at-risk",
          "grid-capacity.specialist-crews-needed",
          "grid-welfare.conduct-welfare-checks",
          "grid-backup.deploy-mobile-generators",
          "grid-safety.advise-on-safe-generator-use",
          "grid-operations.dispatch-specialist-repair-crews",
          "grid-coordination.scale-up-to-regional-crisis-command",
          "grid-information.publish-restoration-estimate-updates"
        ]
      }
