      "template": "Source and cause: {1}; {2}; {3}.\nSupply area and exposure: {4}; {5}; {6}.\nHealth and operational impact: {7}; {8}; {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for fire, police, water operators, public-health, environmental and municipal services. Write an approximately 400-word realistic drinking-water contamination incident for a professional exercise and decision-support briefing. Establish timeline, affected zones and users, operational capacity, uncertainty, health implications and likely developments in a calm, evidence-aware tone. Separate confirmed results from hypotheses. If response or investigation measures are listed, assess suitability, timing, dependencies, coordination, side effects and important gaps; if no measures are listed, describe only the incident and effects and do not invent a solution. Structure the response with an incident overview, operational picture, uncertainties and implications. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Water supply contamination incident example",
        "desc": "<p>A treatment-works fault is first suspected after unusual results are reported from several distribution zones. A security review later identifies suspicious access, so deliberate introduction is being investigated but has not been proved. Hospitals and care settings are among exposed users; illness reports are assessed and the exposure window may be ongoing.</p><p>Laboratory capacity is stretched as teams prioritise samples from the affected works, downstream reservoirs and high-risk facilities. Leads separate confirmed results from preliminary indicators and coordinate water operations, public health, emergency services and local authorities. Affected users need clear instructions that remain valid as results arrive.</p><p>Measures include a do-not-drink notice, tanker refill points, isolation of the affected zone, regional command, prioritised sampling and a targeted area alert. Investigators preserve samples and access logs and coordinate with police to establish responsibility. Authorities verify safety before lifting restrictions and explain restoration decisions.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "cause.deliberate-introduction",
          "contaminant.microbial",
          "entry-point.treatment-works",
          "supply-scope.several-zones",
          "exposed-users.hospitals-and-care-settings",
