      "template": "Incident profile: {1}; {2}; {3}.\nLocation and exposure: {4}; {5}; {6}.\nImpact and capacity: {7}; {8}; {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, public-health and municipal services. Write a realistic incident scenario or decision-support briefing of about 400 words for professional European emergency responders, using only the situation information below. Structure it with a concise incident overview, developing impacts and uncertainty, multi-agency response considerations, and consequences for affected people and essential services. Stay at the level of professional response, protection, investigation and lawful apprehension; do not describe operational attack methods. If response or investigation measures are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps without treating selections as a guaranteed plan. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions for the team.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Terrorist attack (explosive) — exercise briefing",
        "desc": "<p>Emergency services respond to a reported explosive incident at a busy transport interchange. The initial blast has caused local debris damage and injuries, while specialist assessment is still under way and responders are checking for any continuing hazard. The site is temporarily controlled, access is restricted and the casualty demand stretches local response capacity but remains manageable. Command directs a controlled evacuation, search and rescue, and requests explosive ordnance expertise while fire and structural safety are assessed. A multi-agency command coordinates specialist support and verified public advice. Police preserve scene records, secure relevant video, develop a joint intelligence picture and plan a safe, evidence-led apprehension. Public updates avoid unverified claims and protect the integrity of the investigation.</p><p>Command maintains a proportionate safety perimeter, confirms responsibilities across agencies and gives accessible, verified information to people who need to act. Partners preserve decision logs and record uncertainties so that protective actions can be reviewed as evidence develops.</p><p>After immediate life-safety priorities are addressed, the lead authorities coordinate recovery and a lawful investigation. The team reviews the timing and suitability of selected measures, identifies unmet needs and agrees how to adapt if the threat or impact assessment changes.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "event-phase.explosion-or-blast-confirmed",
          "observed-effects.local-blast-or-debris-damage",
          "scene-clearance.specialist-assessment-in-progress",
          "setting.transport-or-public-venue",
          "population-presence.high-occupancy",
          "responder-access.access-restricted",
          "casualty-status.injuries-reported",
          "service-impact.local-disruption",
          "response-capacity.resources-stretched",
          "protective-action.evacuate-threatened-area",
          "life-saving-response.search-and-rescue",
          "specialist-protection.request-explosive-ordnance-specialists",
          "scene-control.establish-an-exclusion-perimeter",
          "command-coordination.activate-multi-agency-command",
          "public-information.send-a-targeted-public-warning",
          "evidence.conduct-specialist-forensic-examination",
          "suspect-tracing.build-a-joint-intelligence-picture",
          "apprehension.plan-safe-controlled-arrest"
        ]
      }
