      "template": "Incident profile: {1}; {2}; {3}.\nLocation and exposure: {4}; {5}; {6}.\nImpact and capacity: {7}; {8}; {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, public-health and municipal services. Write a realistic incident scenario or decision-support briefing of about 400 words for professional European emergency responders, using only the situation information below. Structure it with a concise incident overview, developing impacts and uncertainty, multi-agency response considerations, and consequences for affected people and essential services. Stay at the level of professional response, protection, investigation and lawful apprehension; do not describe operational attack methods. If response or investigation measures are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps without treating selections as a guaranteed plan. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions for the team.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Active shooter / Armed assault — exercise briefing",
        "desc": "<p>Police and emergency services respond to an armed assault report at a public venue. The threat is contained but a suspect remains outstanding; responders report injuries, while access to the scene is restricted and local resources are stretched. Command directs people along controlled safe routes, establishes a protected casualty collection point and coordinates urgent medical care. A controlled perimeter preserves emergency routes, and a unified command requests specialist police and health support. Verified public updates provide safety advice without disclosing sensitive operational information. Police secure scene records and relevant video, coordinate witness accounts and lawful enquiries, and plan a safe controlled arrest with appropriate custody and safeguarding.</p><p>Incident command maintains proportionate safety controls, confirms responsibilities across agencies and gives accessible, verified information to people who need to act. Partners record decisions and uncertainties so that protective actions can be reviewed as evidence develops.</p><p>After immediate life-safety priorities are addressed, the lead authorities coordinate recovery and a lawful investigation. The team reviews the timing and suitability of selected measures, identifies unmet needs and agrees how to adapt if the threat or impact assessment changes.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "threat-status.threat-contained-suspect-outstanding",
          "incident-scope.threat-near-a-public-gathering",
          "scene-release.scene-controlled-for-response",
          "setting.transport-or-public-venue",
          "population-presence.high-occupancy",
          "responder-access.access-restricted",
          "casualty-status.injuries-reported",
          "service-impact.local-disruption",
          "response-capacity.resources-stretched",
          "protective-action.evacuate-by-a-controlled-safe-route",
          "life-saving-response.triage-and-casualty-collection",
          "specialist-protection.set-up-a-safe-casualty-collection-point",
          "scene-control.establish-a-controlled-perimeter",
          "command-coordination.activate-multi-agency-command",
          "public-information.provide-regular-verified-updates",
          "evidence.secure-relevant-video-and-digital-records",
          "suspect-tracing.build-a-joint-intelligence-picture",
          "apprehension.plan-safe-controlled-arrest"
        ]
      }
