      "example": {
        "label": "Disorder after a contested local decision",
        "desc": "<p>Following a contested public decision, a large gathering forms in the town centre. Most participants remain peaceful, while a smaller group becomes involved in isolated confrontations and damage near a transport interchange. The crowd moves along several streets and the situation continues into the evening.</p><p>A small number of people require medical attention. Local transport and access are disrupted, and the initial response is stretched while regional support is mobilised. Residents need clear advice, and emergency routes must remain available without treating the wider gathering as unlawful.</p><p>The response establishes a safe area and first-aid point, protects the damaged site, and uses dialogue-led policing with targeted intervention for specific violence. Verified diversions and multi-agency updates are issued. Investigators preserve relevant footage and witness accounts and prepare evidence-led cases for any arrests made on lawful grounds.</p>",
