      "template": "Incident profile: {1}; {2}; {3}.\nLocation and exposure: {4}; {5}; {6}.\nImpact and capacity: {7}; {8}; {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, public-health and municipal services. Write a realistic incident scenario or decision-support briefing of about 400 words for professional European emergency responders, using only the situation information below. Structure it with a concise incident overview, developing impacts and uncertainty, multi-agency response considerations, and consequences for affected people and essential services. Stay at the level of professional response, protection, investigation and lawful apprehension; do not describe operational attack methods. If response or investigation measures are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps without treating selections as a guaranteed plan. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions for the team.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Drone attack — exercise briefing",
        "desc": "<p>An incident is reported near a critical facility after hostile drone-related activity is confirmed. There is local damage and a possible secondary hazard; people are moved to a safe reception point while responders establish controlled safety zones and request specialist assessment. The facility’s operations are disrupted, and local resources are stretched. A multi-agency command brings police, fire, health, aviation and infrastructure partners together; temporary local airspace restrictions and verified public advice are coordinated according to the evolving assessment. Investigators preserve the scene, secure relevant video and technical records, develop a joint intelligence picture and coordinate lawful suspect tracing and safe apprehension. No one is asked to approach or handle an unknown object.</p><p>Incident command maintains proportionate safety controls, confirms responsibilities across agencies and gives accessible, verified information to people who need to act. Partners record decisions and uncertainties so that protective actions can be reviewed as evidence develops.</p><p>After immediate life-safety priorities are addressed, the lead authorities coordinate recovery and a lawful investigation. The team reviews the timing and suitability of selected measures, identifies unmet needs and agrees how to adapt if the threat or impact assessment changes.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "activity-status.hostile-activity-confirmed",
          "observed-effects.local-impact-or-damage",
          "hazard-assessment.secondary-hazard-suspected",
          "setting.industrial-or-critical-site",
          "population-presence.moderate-occupancy",
          "responder-access.access-restricted",
          "casualty-status.injuries-reported",
          "service-impact.critical-services-disrupted",
          "response-capacity.resources-stretched",
          "protective-action.move-people-to-a-safe-reception-point",
          "life-saving-response.triage-and-casualty-collection",
          "specialist-protection.request-specialist-explosive-or-hazardous-material-assessment",
          "scene-control.establish-a-controlled-scene-perimeter",
          "command-coordination.activate-multi-agency-command",
          "public-information.provide-regular-verified-updates",
          "evidence.secure-relevant-video-and-digital-records",
          "suspect-tracing.build-a-joint-intelligence-picture",
          "apprehension.plan-safe-controlled-arrest"
        ]
      }
