      "template": "The incident context is {1}, {2} and {3}.\nThe location and exposure are {4}, {5} and {6}.\nThe operational impact is {7}, {8} and {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for emergency services, infrastructure operators and public authorities. Write a realistic exercise or decision-support briefing of about 400 words for incident commanders and relevant partner leads. Use the selected situation values as the factual frame, distinguish confirmed information from uncertainty, and structure the account as incident onset, context and exposure, effects on people and services, response pressures, and near-term outlook. Keep the account at professional response-planning level and do not provide instructions that would enable harm. If measures (including investigation measures) are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects and identify important gaps. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. End with two reflection or exercise questions.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Hybrid threat exercise",
        "desc": "<p>A developing hybrid threat incident is characterised by Coordinated multi-domain activity, Digital service disruption, Immediate activity disrupted, Critical infrastructure, National service exposure, Digital and communications services, Essential service disruption, Several sectors affected, Specialist resources stretched. Early reports do not yet establish its full scope or cause. The incident lead verifies immediate exposure with service owners and partner agencies, records confirmed facts separately from working assumptions, and protects people who may be at risk.</p><p>Response teams maintain a shared picture of impacts, dependencies and available capacity. They select Issue proportionate protective advice, Verify reports through trusted channels, Review dependencies and staged recovery, Convene strategic threat assessment, Maintain a verified shared situation picture, Publish verified facts and correction updates to support safe operations and communicate verified information through appropriate channels. Measures are sequenced as conditions change, with attention to service continuity, evidence integrity and public confidence.</p><p>Investigation measures include Preserve relevant digital and physical records, Assess attribution with competent specialists, Refer evidence for law-enforcement investigation. Competent authorities coordinate attribution and lawful tracing without premature conclusions, and pursue apprehension, disruption or prosecution through appropriate routes. The exercise tests how operational leaders balance immediate protection, restoration and accountability as new information emerges.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "hyb-event.1",
          "hyb-target.2",
          "hyb-status.3",
          "hyb-setting.2",
