      "template": "The incident context is {1}, {2} and {3}.\nThe location and exposure are {4}, {5} and {6}.\nThe operational impact is {7}, {8} and {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced crisis-management trainer for emergency services, infrastructure operators and public authorities. Write a realistic exercise or decision-support briefing of about 400 words for incident commanders and relevant partner leads. Use the selected situation values as the factual frame, distinguish confirmed information from uncertainty, and structure the account as incident onset, context and exposure, effects on people and services, response pressures, and near-term outlook. Keep the account at professional response-planning level and do not provide instructions that would enable harm. If measures (including investigation measures) are listed, assess their suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects and identify important gaps. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. End with two reflection or exercise questions.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Intentional supply-chain disruption exercise",
        "desc": "<p>A developing intentional supply-chain disruption incident is characterised by Physical interference, Transport and logistics, Active disruption confirmed, Transport corridor, Regional distribution exposure, Medical or public health goods, Shortage of essential supplies, Regional network affected, Reserves under pressure. Early reports do not yet establish its full scope or cause. The incident lead verifies immediate exposure with service owners and partner agencies, records confirmed facts separately from working assumptions, and protects people who may be at risk.</p><p>Response teams maintain a shared picture of impacts, dependencies and available capacity. They select Protect staff and secure exposed deliveries, Inspect suspect consignments through authorised procedures, Use qualified substitute suppliers, Convene regional logistics coordination, Coordinate with emergency services and public authorities, Issue public advice on verified shortages to support safe operations and communicate verified information through appropriate channels. Measures are sequenced as conditions change, with attention to service continuity, evidence integrity and public confidence.</p><p>Investigation measures include Preserve shipment and procurement records, Trace supplier and logistics links with investigators, Support lawful suspect apprehension. Competent authorities coordinate attribution and lawful tracing without premature conclusions, and pursue apprehension, disruption or prosecution through appropriate routes. The exercise tests how operational leaders balance immediate protection, restoration and accountability as new information emerges.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "sup-event.2",
          "sup-target.2",
          "sup-status.2",
          "sup-setting.2",
          "sup-exposure.2",
          "sup-dependency.2",
          "sup-impact.2",
          "sup-scale.2",
          "sup-capacity.2",
          "sup-life-safety.1",
          "sup-contain.1",
          "sup-continuity.2",
          "sup-command.2",
          "sup-liaison.2",
          "sup-warning.2",
          "sup-evidence.1",
          "sup-trace.1",
          "sup-enforce.1"
        ]
      }
    },
