      "template": "A {1} is reported at a {2}, with a pattern of {3}.\nOccupancy is {4}; nearby exposure is {5}, and spread conditions are {6}.\nThe life-safety impact is {7}; services are {8}, and fire response capacity is {9}.",
      "prompt": "You are an experienced fire-service and crisis-management trainer for fire, police, medical, utility and municipal partners. Write an approximately 400-word professional British-English incident narrative for an exercise and decision-support briefing, using all selected situation values without contradicting them. Describe chronology, site and exposure, people affected, fire conditions, service impacts, uncertainty and response capacity; distinguish verified facts from reports and avoid prejudging attribution. If containment or investigation measures are listed, assess suitability, timing, dependencies and side effects, and identify important gaps. Prioritise life safety, proportionate fire control, continuity of essential services, scene safety and evidence-led lawful investigation. If no measures are listed, describe only the incident and do not invent a solution. Structure the account as a situation overview, developing impacts and decision points, then an assessment. End with exactly two reflection or exercise questions.",
      "example": {
        "label": "Deliberate fire at a public building",
        "desc": "<p>Smoke and heat are reported at an occupied public building after closing time, and an active fire may spread to an adjacent block. A small number of people are treated for smoke exposure while the remaining occupants are accounted for. Dry, windy conditions increase the risk to nearby buildings, and local access is affected.</p><p>Fire and rescue crews establish incident command, search occupied areas and conduct a supported evacuation. Crews protect adjacent premises, isolate affected utilities safely and keep appliance routes clear. Local smoke-safety and evacuation information is issued through verified channels, while temporary accommodation is coordinated for displaced residents.</p><p>After the scene is safe, investigators protect it for examination, document damage and preserve relevant camera records. Witness accounts and forensic findings are assessed together, and any suspect action is referred through lawful procedures. The response balances immediate life safety, fire control, service continuity and an evidence-led investigation.</p>",
        "choices": [
          "fire-state.active-fire-and-spread-possible",
          "site-type.commercial-or-public-premises",
          "incident-pattern.single-fire-location",
          "occupancy.people-may-remain-inside",
          "surroundings.dense-buildings-or-vegetation",
          "fire-weather.dry-or-windy-conditions",
          "life-safety-impact.people-treated-or-displaced",
          "service-impact.local-access-or-utilities-disrupted",
          "fire-response-capacity.additional-crews-mobilising",
          "rescue-and-evacuation.conduct-supported-evacuation",
          "fire-suppression.deploy-structural-firefighting-crews",
          "utilities-and-recovery.isolate-affected-utilities-safely",
          "fire-service-coordination.establish-incident-command",
          "access-management.keep-appliance-access-routes-clear",
          "public-warning.issue-local-smoke-safety-advice",
          "fire-evidence.preserve-relevant-cctv-or-access-records",
          "suspect-identification.review-verified-camera-footage",
          "lawful-apprehension.refer-to-specialist-investigators"
        ]
